ategory_count":4},{"business_id":"_Bi9kN_eR75G1eqIl7S3pA","name":"The Bulldog","shared_categories":"Bars, Food, Nightlife","shared_category_count":3},{"business_id":"AU-B663F3MPO7W-goWwwXA","name":"B Mac's","shared_categories":"Bars, Nightlife","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"_C7QiQQc47AOEv4PE3Kong","name":"Commander's Palace","shared_categories":"Bars, Nightlife","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"JhpRI9m71ybWHkAqRdL0Tg","name":"The Avenue Pub","shared_categories":"Bars, Nightlife","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"pKykk7lnD6Tf9wSzJYRyJA","name":"Starbucks","shared_categories":"Food","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"TMBbCDQG6bENJoQSST0XiA","name":"Brigtsen's Restaurant","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0},{"business_id":"mhrW9O0O5hXGXGnEYBVoag","name":"Jacques-Imo's Cafe","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0},{"business_id":"8KnMSrMuTI2AtHZ2LOI8OQ","name":"Maurepas Foods","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0},{"business_id":"Zi-F-YvyVOK0k5QD7lrLOg","name":"Muriel's Jackson Square","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0}],"text":[{"business_id":"PjpfBYGzQj6fdiuf4tNLsg","review_id":"lU8BQ6iOIQ3M99yJy9QIRQ","date":"2021-05-09T03:39:11","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.943194568157196,"text_excerpt":"I husband and I saw the beer slushies offered at Miel on social media, and wanted to come by and check it out. Such a cute place! The patio is really pretty and had ample tables without being too crowded. There was decent music that was the perfect volume. The variety of beers was nice, and they weren't cheap but were definitely quality. The flavors were unique and bold. We loved the mango beer slushie, the flor de Jamaica beer, and the mammoth lavender beer. The bartenders were also friendly. I look forward to coming back!"},{"business_id":"PjpfBYGzQj6fdiuf4tNLsg","review_id":"IEnX0Q_hYHN8ZquPcwODXA","date":"2021-08-12T21:30:36","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9318360090255737,"text_excerpt":"Miel is my favorite brewery in New Orleans. It's woman owned, the name literally means \"honey,\" there's a DISCO BALL, and often there is a projector and controls to play MARIO KART. There's a small selection of board/card games you can play on the tables inside, the picnic tables outside, and bar seating. The mural outside is down by a young local artist. There's a rotating selection of interesting, fun, but not lofty, beers on tap and I haven't found one I didn't like. It's worth it to get as many different small pours as you can. There's also usually a delicious pop up food vendor, along with a consistent coffee pop up on the weekends."},{"business_id":"PjpfBYGzQj6fdiuf4tNLsg","review_id":"HxfFR7BhWmOIqH8tostX1A","date":"2018-11-19T20:37:52","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.930033802986145,"text_excerpt":"Very cool, hipster brewery with delicious beers on tap. We've been anticipating this one for a while, since they were gonna attempt some mead and honey beer. Alas, the alcohol content was a bit too high for that avenue, so like a good brewery - they improvised! And did NOT disappoint. Looks like it's gonna be a great spot for trivia, movies, Saints games, birthdays, and just good 'ole regular beer drinking. They have food pop-ups and are completely CASHLESS. Yep, credit card only. Lots of yard games to keep you busy. Crisp and clean spot, that doesn't feel like your typical warehouse brewery."}],"visual":[{"business_id":"PjpfBYGzQj6fdiuf4tNLsg","photo_id":"SzWrR1VkhC3R-JqnonOTdw","label":"inside","image_url":"/photos/SzWrR1VkhC3R-JqnonOTdw.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.8923969268798828},{"business_id":"PjpfBYGzQj6fdiuf4tNLsg","photo_id":"5WVHk2FeARSWPRPoXcr0KQ","label":"drink","image_url":"/photos/5WVHk2FeARSWPRPoXcr0KQ.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.8886702060699463},{"business_id":"PjpfBYGzQj6fdiuf4tNLsg","photo_id":"Kf3DIRQ_B217mnJ_Cci91Q","label":"inside","image_url":"/photos/Kf3DIRQ_B217mnJ_Cci91Q.jpg","visual_representativen